<title>MEXICO: Mexico crude port Dos Bocas reopens - port.</title>
<headline>Mexico crude port Dos Bocas reopens - port.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexican crude port Dos Bocas in Tabasco state reopened to crude shipments at 1300 local/1800 GMT on Tuesday as weather improved in the Gulf of Mexico, a port official said.</p>
<p>Waves up to 12 feet high had relaxed at the site, he said. Three crude tankers that had been stuck at the port set sail after the opening, he told Reuters.  </p>
<p>The port originally closed on Sunday at 2200 local/0300 GMT amid regional storms.</p>
<p>Dos Bocas exported an average of 505,900 barrels per day (bpd) in 1996, Pajaritos exported an average 416,200 bpd and Cayo Arcas shipped about 576,300 bpd, according to the latest Pemex figures.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
